spec:
  grid: 13x13 [observed, all examples identical]
  base_colors: black (0) and blue (1) fill entire grid except marker pixels
  blue_walls:
    role: 4-connected path/chain structures that partition the black background into regions
    components: 1-5, total 43-50 cells (25-30% of grid)
    topology: mostly degree-2 chains (78-95%), endpoints 2-10, branch points 0-2
  black_regions:
    count: 3-5 components via 4-connectivity
    size_range: 2-110 cells; one large exterior region + smaller interior pockets
  markers:
    count: 3-7 pixels total, 3-6 distinct colors from {2..9}
    duplicate: at most 1 color appears twice; rest are unique
    placement: each replaces a black cell; neighbors are only black and/or blue (never another marker)
  constraint: every black and blue 4-connected component must be side-adjacent to >=1 marker
  transform:
    recolor each black/blue component with the marker color having max shared-edge contact
    ties broken by row-major marker position (top-left wins)
    marker pixels preserved in output; output contains only marker colors

generation_strategy:
  approach: direct construction with validation
  steps:
    1. Start with 13x13 black grid
    2. Draw 1-5 blue (1) path/chain structures using random walks on the grid;
       paths should be mostly degree-2 (no thick blobs), total ~45 blue cells
    3. Choose 3-6 distinct marker colors from {2..9}; optionally duplicate one
    4. Label all black and blue 4-connected components
    5. Place markers one at a time on black cells, ensuring each is adjacent
       to at least one base-color component that lacks a marker neighbor;
       some markers should be placed adjacent to blue walls (on the boundary)
    6. Validate every component touches >=1 marker; reject if not
    7. Run solver to verify non-trivial output (multiple colors in result)

